---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import Section from '../../components/Section.astro';
import Ladder from '../../components/Ladder.astro';
import Tiles from '../../components/Tiles.astro';
import BookButton from '../../components/BookButton.astro';
import Photo from '../../components/Photo.astro';
import flightPhoto from '../../assets/photos/glider-in-flight.jpg';
import { facts, fees, num, money } from '../../lib/facts';
import { href } from '../../lib/url';

const a = facts.achievements;
const m = fees.membership;
const rungs = [
  { name: 'First solo', detail: `from age ${facts.training.solo_age}` },
  { name: 'An hour aloft', detail: 'your first real soaring flight' },
  { name: 'Cross-country', detail: 'leaving the home field behind' },
  ...facts.badges,
];
---
<Base
  title="Why gliding? A sport you never finish"
  description="Gliding is to powered flying what sailing is to motorboating. Every flight is a puzzle, there is always a next step, and you can do it for decades."
>
  <PageHero label="Why gliding?" title="A sport you never finish">
    <p class="lead">Gliding is to powered flying what sailing is to motorboating. With an engine, the flying serves the trip. In a glider, the flying is the game.</p>
    <div class="actions"><BookButton /></div>
    <Photo slot="media" src={flightPhoto} alt="A club glider flies low over the field against towering white cumulus clouds" crop="4 / 3" position="65% center" eager />
  </PageHero>

  <Section variant="plain" labelledby="game-h">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h2 id="game-h">The game</h2>
        <p>There is no throttle, so every flight is a puzzle: find rising air, climb in it, decide where to go next. The sky changes by the hour. Some days it gives you 10 minutes, some days 10 hours.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="dec-h">A sport for decades</h2>
        <p>Gliding rewards judgment more than strength, so a 16-year-old and a 70-year-old fly the same sky. And nobody launches alone: it takes a crew, which is why it works as a club.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section labelledby="reach-h">
    <div class="grid grid--2">
      <div>
        <h2 id="reach-h">Within reach</h2>
        <p>Club instructors teach you for free. Members pay {money(fees.winch_launch)} a launch and {money(fees.glider_rental_per_hour)} an hour of glider time, billed by the minute: about {money(fees.typical_lesson_flight.cost)} for a typical {fees.typical_lesson_flight.minutes}-minute instructional flight. Membership is {money(m.youth_air_cadet.price)} to {money(m.regular.price)} a year.</p>
        <p><a class="more" href={href('/costs/')}>See all costs</a></p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h2 id="better-h">It makes better pilots</h2>
        <p>Gliding builds stick-and-rudder skill and energy management like nothing else. The captains of both the “Miracle on the Hudson” and the “Gimli Glider” were glider pilots.</p>
        <p><a class="more" href={href('/learn-to-fly/power-pilots/')}>Already a power pilot?</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Section labelledby="rung-h">
    <h2 id="rung-h">Always a next rung</h2>
    <Ladder rungs={rungs} />
  </Section>

  <Section labelledby="race-h">
    <h2 id="race-h">And then there's racing</h2>
    <p>Cross-country gliding is also a race: fly a set course around turnpoints, and the fastest average speed wins. Any flight can be scored online and ranked against pilots around the world.</p>
    <Tiles
      items={[
        { figure: `${num(a.longest_cross_country_km)} km`, text: `the longest cross-country flight out of ${facts.club.short_name}` },
        { figure: `${a.long_flight_hours} hours`, text: `aloft on a single flight out of ${facts.club.short_name}` },
        { figure: `${num(a.world_distance_record_km)} km`, text: 'the world distance record' },
      ]}
    />
    <div class="actions"><BookButton /></div>
  </Section>
</Base>
